From: DHB_AX local port <local@invalid>
Subject: [LOCAL ONLY] net: stmmac: size the Hi3531 RX ring for burst receive

The Hi3531 receive engine cannot be restarted once it suspends for want of
a receive descriptor.  When the ring runs dry the DMA sets RU in CSR5 and
moves the receive process to state 4, and from there it ignores a receive
poll demand, ignores the DMA start/stop bit, ignores the MAC receiver
enable, and survives both a channel software reset and a full interface
down/up.  Only a software reset of all three DMA channels clears it, which
is why hi3531_reset_dma_channels() exists for the probe path.

Descriptor exhaustion is therefore not a recoverable condition on this
SoC, and it is reachable: with the DWMAC1000 default of 512 descriptors a
four-stream inbound TCP test wedges the interface within the first
seconds, after 40-110 MB.  Receive checksum offload is unavailable here,
so every byte is summed on the CPU and a scheduling delay long enough to
drain the ring is easy to hit.

Doubling the ring to the 1024 the core allows removes the exhaustion.  The
same test then sustains 1.52 GB, and a 900 Mbit/s UDP flood sustains
6.29 GB offered, without the RU bit being set once.

The size is a module parameter because characterising the approach to
exhaustion means sweeping it, and ethtool -G is not usable for that: on a
healthy interface it wedges receive by a second route, leaving CSR19
walking addresses outside the ring CSR3 points at.

This does not repair the underlying fault; it keeps the driver away from
the state that triggers it.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-hi3531.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-hi3531.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-hi3531.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-hi3531.c
@@ -68,6 +68,11 @@
 #define HI3531_GMAC_IF_SPEED_10		0x1
 #define HI3531_GMAC_IF_SPEED_100	0x3
 
+static unsigned int rx_ring_size = DMA_MAX_RX_SIZE;
+module_param(rx_ring_size, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_ring_size,
+		 "receive descriptors per ring, 64 to 1024 (default 1024)");
+
 struct hi3531_dwmac {
 	struct device *dev;
 	void __iomem *gmac;
@@ -114,6 +119,16 @@ static struct mac_device_info *hi3531_dwmac_setup(void *arg)
 	mac->pcsr = priv->ioaddr + HI3531_GMAC1_MAC_OFFSET;
 	priv->dmaaddr = priv->ioaddr + HI3531_GMAC1_DMA_OFFSET;
 
+	/*
+	 * A receive process that suspends for want of a descriptor on this
+	 * SoC cannot be resumed: poll demand, the DMA start bit, the MAC
+	 * receiver enable and a channel software reset all leave it in state
+	 * 4, and only a reset of all three DMA channels recovers it.  Carry
+	 * enough descriptors that an inbound burst does not empty the ring
+	 * while a CPU busy with software checksums is late to refill it.
+	 */
+	priv->dma_conf.dma_rx_size = rx_ring_size;
+
 	return mac;
 }
 
@@ -239,6 +254,13 @@ static int hi3531_dwmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct hi3531_dwmac *dwmac;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (rx_ring_size < DMA_MIN_RX_SIZE || rx_ring_size > DMA_MAX_RX_SIZE) {
+		dev_err(&pdev->dev,
+			"rx_ring_size %u is outside %u-%u\n", rx_ring_size,
+			DMA_MIN_RX_SIZE, DMA_MAX_RX_SIZE);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	ret = stmmac_get_platform_resources(pdev, &res);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
